    <Callout type="tip" title="Why isolated agents matter">
      Agents marked "Worktree" run in separate context windows. All their research tokens, documentation fetches, and analysis stay outside your main session. Only the distilled output enters your primary context &mdash; saving thousands of tokens per session.
    </Callout>

    <!-- SKILLS -->
    <h3 id="skills">Skills System (Slash Commands)</h3>

    <Callout type="tip" title="What are slash commands?">
      Slash commands are the <strong>buttons</strong> you press to make VibeCrew do things. You type a command starting with <code>/</code> (like <code>/new-project</code> or <code>/wrap</code>) and VibeCrew handles the rest. Each command triggers a specific workflow &mdash; some are simple (like <code>/idea</code> which just saves a note) and some are complex (like <code>/new-project</code> which orchestrates multiple agents over 6 steps). You don't need to know how they work internally, just what they do and when to use them.
    </Callout>

    <p>Every slash command in VibeCrew is implemented as a <strong>skill</strong> &mdash; a <code>SKILL.md</code> file in the <code>skills/</code> directory. Skills are the primary user-facing interface to the system.</p>

    <h4>How skills work</h4>
    <div class="flow"><span class="highlight">User types:</span> /new-feature "user-auth"
    &darr;
Claude Code discovers <span class="highlight">skills/new-feature/SKILL.md</span>
    &darr;
Reads YAML frontmatter:
  name: new-feature
  description: Start a new feature
  args: feature_name
    &darr;
Expands SKILL.md body as agent instructions
    &darr;
<span class="highlight">Skill executes:</span> precondition checks, state mutations, agent handoffs
    &darr;
<span class="muted">Results written to .vibecrew/ state files</span></div>

    <h4>Skill definition format</h4>
    <p>Each skill is a Markdown file with YAML frontmatter. The body contains the full workflow: preconditions, step-by-step execution, error handling, state mutations, and agent handoffs.</p>

    <pre><code><span class="code-label">skills/new-feature/SKILL.md</span>---
name: new-feature
description: Start a new feature session on a dedicated branch
args: feature_name
---

# /new-feature workflow

1. Check foundation is complete (read state.json)
2. Check WIP limits (max 2 in-progress features)
3. Find or create feature in backlog.json
4. Create git branch: feat/&#123;feature_name&#125;
5. Create safety checkpoint
6. Initialize 6-phase tracking in state.json
7. Hand off to Builder agent</code></pre>

