            <td><strong>SessionStart</strong></td>
            <td><code>session-startup.sh</code>, <code>sync-state.sh</code>, <code>error-recovery.sh</code></td>
            <td>Every Claude Code start</td>
            <td>Environment check, state reconciliation, clear stale locks</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>SessionStart</strong> (compact)</td>
            <td><code>compact-reinject.sh</code></td>
            <td>After context compaction</td>
            <td>Re-injects project state after context compaction</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>PreToolUse</strong> (Write/Edit)</td>
            <td><code>phase-gate.sh</code>, <code>restrict-paths.sh</code></td>
            <td>Before any file write</td>
            <td>Blocks source writes before foundation; validates write targets</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>PreToolUse</strong> (Bash)</td>
            <td><code>protect-data.sh</code></td>
            <td>Before any shell command</td>
            <td>Blocks destructive operations (rm -rf, DROP TABLE, force push)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>PostToolUse</strong> (Write/Edit)</td>
            <td><code>format-code.sh</code></td>
            <td>After every file write</td>
            <td>Auto-formats with Prettier, Black, rustfmt, gofmt</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Notification</strong></td>
            <td><code>notify.sh</code></td>
            <td>Permission blocked or task complete</td>
            <td>Sends native OS notification with Warp deep-link</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>PostToolUseFailure</strong></td>
            <td><code>notify.sh error</code></td>
            <td>Any tool execution fails</td>
            <td>Sends error notification</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Stop</strong></td>
            <td><code>check-context.sh</code>, <code>cost-guardrails.sh</code>, <code>claude-md-lint.sh</code>, <code>quality-gate.sh</code></td>
            <td>Session ending</td>
            <td>Context warnings, cost threshold checks, CLAUDE.md validation, typecheck/lint/build on modified files</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <h4>How hooks enforce behavior</h4>
    <p>When Claude Code encounters a lifecycle event, it checks <code>hooks.json</code> for matching entries, passes a JSON payload to the script via stdin, and reads the exit code. <strong>Exit 0</strong> = allow the operation. <strong>Exit 2</strong> = block the operation. This gives hooks the power to both observe (PostToolUse) and control (PreToolUse) agent behavior.</p>

    <!-- SCRIPTS -->
    <h3 id="scripts">Scripts Reference</h3>

    <Callout type="tip" title="What are scripts?">
      Scripts are the <strong>worker bees</strong> of VibeCrew. While agents think and make decisions, scripts do the actual mechanical work: creating files, updating project state, calculating scores, sending notifications. They're small programs that run in milliseconds and always produce the same result for the same input. This makes VibeCrew predictable and reliable &mdash; the creative AI work is separated from the bookkeeping, so nothing gets lost or corrupted.
    </Callout>

    <p>VibeCrew includes ~67 bash scripts in the <code>scripts/</code> directory. Every state mutation goes through a script &mdash; agents never write <code>.vibecrew/</code> files directly. Scripts are organized by function:</p>

